WEBVTT

00:00.516 --> 00:04.422
And we're going to excuse Mayor Gray and Ben

00:04.470 --> 00:08.182
Reeves, our city manager, because they are in New York

00:08.682 --> 00:11.876
right now attending to some city business to help us with some things that we're

00:11.957 --> 00:15.118
working on. We're going to move into the Pledge of Allegiance,

00:15.199 --> 00:17.940
and I will lead you in that. Please join me for the Pledge of Allegiance.

00:20.618 --> 00:24.094
I pledge allegiance to the flag of the United States of

00:24.594 --> 00:27.220
America and to the republic for which it stands. I pledge allegiance to the flag

00:27.720 --> 00:27.880
of the United States of America, and to the republic for which it stands,

00:28.380 --> 00:31.620
one nation under God, indivisible, with liberty

00:32.120 --> 00:33.790
and justice for all.

00:37.120 --> 00:40.440
Okay, so this afternoon's meeting is going

00:40.940 --> 00:44.120
to be short and sweet. It was something that we needed to call a special

00:44.620 --> 00:48.620
meeting for because of some timelines and deadlines.

00:49.120 --> 00:52.580
So we will be looking at a resolution of

00:53.080 --> 00:57.161
Eagle Mountain City, Utah, protesting The Red Cedar Corporation annexation

00:57.661 --> 01:01.032
petition filed with the Town of Cedar Fort on July 27th,

01:01.096 --> 01:04.725
2026. And I'll invite Marcus to

01:05.225 --> 01:09.607
present the item. Yes, so we became aware of this, I believe yesterday,

01:09.929 --> 01:13.895
that the petition for annexation was filed under

01:13.927 --> 01:16.963
state code. Prior to even filing the petition,

01:17.701 --> 01:21.122
the petitioner should have sent a notice of intent to file a petition with

01:21.154 --> 01:24.717
us. Because we are an affected entity, and that is one

01:25.217 --> 01:27.719
of the procedural problems with their petition.

01:28.938 --> 01:33.111
So we drafted a protest letter because this overlaps

01:33.611 --> 01:36.722
with our annexation policy plan expansion area, and and we

01:37.222 --> 01:40.606
have some interest in potentially annexing a portion of that

01:41.553 --> 01:43.800
proposed annexation into Eagle Mountain City.

01:44.362 --> 01:46.577
Additionally, we've had contact with.

01:47.735 --> 01:51.192
the representatives of several of the landowners that are proposed to

01:51.224 --> 01:54.600
be annexed into Cedar Fort, and they do not desire to be annexed into Cedar

01:55.100 --> 01:58.804
Fort and are very troubled by this petition.

01:58.917 --> 02:02.765
So we are filing as an affected entity. We have standing

02:02.781 --> 02:06.346
to file a protest, and that's what this would be, a resolution to do

02:06.846 --> 02:10.179
that. Thank you. Just— and I'd like to recognize

02:10.211 --> 02:13.383
that Mayor Gray and Ben Reeves are

02:13.400 --> 02:17.173
both online, but because they're remote, I'll continue

02:17.673 --> 02:20.491
to conduct the meeting unless the mayor tells me otherwise. Um,

02:20.750 --> 02:24.392
does council have any questions about the item that is at hand?

02:27.990 --> 02:30.282
This is Craig. I have no questions. Okay.

02:31.063 --> 02:32.428
Council Member Hewish, do you have any questions?

02:35.713 --> 02:39.682
I think, uh, this, this is just a procedural step

02:40.182 --> 02:44.249
in a protest. What, what is the next step after the protest is filed?

02:45.212 --> 02:48.162
Yeah, so we'll file the protest with the Utah County Clerk,

02:49.524 --> 02:52.906
after which the Boundary Commission would have to set a date

02:53.406 --> 02:55.808
for a public hearing, and we would have the opportunity to present at that hearing.

02:56.433 --> 03:00.489
And then they would make a decision on how to recommend,

03:00.841 --> 03:04.112
you know, what Cedar Fort does. My reading of the

03:04.612 --> 03:09.337
laws is not actually binding on the town of Cedar Fort, but it

03:09.837 --> 03:13.265
would certainly bear a lot of persuasive weight. We would have, if they went

03:13.765 --> 03:16.375
forth with the annexation, then we would have to look at other legal recourse if

03:16.875 --> 03:20.126
they chose not to follow the Boundary Commission's recommendation.

03:20.895 --> 03:24.262
Okay. Councilmember Wood, do you have anything that you'd like to share?

03:25.368 --> 03:28.847
Nope. All right. So with that, if no one else

03:28.959 --> 03:32.230
has any other items— oh, okay. Steve.

03:32.679 --> 03:35.789
Just, uh, Marcus can clarify for me, but it

03:36.289 --> 03:39.925
appears unless Cedar Fort changes their mind,

03:40.021 --> 03:44.109
on September 15th they will still have a public hearing on this. They can't move

03:44.609 --> 03:47.235
forward with the public hearing while there's a pending protest.

03:48.030 --> 03:51.429
Okay, what I read in state code was that they can

03:51.445 --> 03:54.796
have the public hearing, they can deny the application, but they can't approve it.

03:54.861 --> 03:57.661
Yes, I mean, that's a little bit more, I guess,

03:57.855 --> 04:01.699
precise. Yes, they could deny the annexation petition

04:01.796 --> 04:04.816
without waiting for the protest to play out, and that would moot the protest,

04:05.558 --> 04:08.048
but they can't approve it until the protest plays out.

04:10.120 --> 04:13.005
Marcus, maybe I have one question. How is it that they can,

04:13.626 --> 04:17.171
Force a landowner to be part of an annexation application

04:17.671 --> 04:20.780
against their will? That is one of the problems with the

04:21.101 --> 04:24.374
petition. Under state law, you need

04:24.874 --> 04:27.999
to have landowners covering at least 50% of the total

04:28.499 --> 04:32.025
area within the annexation, proposed annexation area, that signed the petition.

04:32.073 --> 04:35.538
And my understanding is that did not occur here, that it was only

04:36.038 --> 04:39.356
the Red Cedar Corporation who was the petitioner. They're the only ones that signed it,

04:39.372 --> 04:41.794
and they own approximately a third of the land area, and none of the other

04:42.294 --> 04:44.521
landowners, most of which are associated with the Holbrooks,

04:46.191 --> 04:49.291
And they none of them signed it. It's my is my understanding,

04:50.704 --> 04:54.430
and so that is one of the procedural

04:54.478 --> 04:57.915
problems is that it's the petition's invalid because it doesn't have the

04:58.415 --> 05:01.946
adequate signatures. That being said, my reading of state law

05:02.171 --> 05:06.395
is if you do meet the requirements and have 50%

05:07.070 --> 05:10.619
of the landowners sign, say the landowner is covering 50% of

05:11.119 --> 05:14.633
the total area, and that covers one third of the total value. If you meet

05:15.133 --> 05:18.305
both those requirements and a couple other minor procedural requirements,

05:18.545 --> 05:22.249
you could force other landowners into an annexation

05:22.749 --> 05:25.504
into a municipality that they don't want to be annexed into. So that is something

05:26.004 --> 05:28.630
that is allowable under state law, but not under these circumstances.

05:29.400 --> 05:32.799
Is the reason that they're being included in this is because their property

05:32.815 --> 05:36.663
lies between the applicant and the city that

05:37.163 --> 05:41.072
they want to annex to? So in this area, there is a,

05:41.168 --> 05:45.276
I guess, a corridor, if you will, of parcels that

05:45.324 --> 05:49.001
are between Cedar Fort and Eagle Mountain and within unincorporated Utah County.

05:49.531 --> 05:52.903
The Red Cedar Corporation parcels are actually just to the north of this corridor.

05:54.236 --> 05:57.784
And all the ones to the south are, again, most of them are

05:58.284 --> 06:02.120
associated with the Holbrook family. And I

06:02.280 --> 06:05.251
can't, I mean, I have ideas, but I don't know what their motives are for

06:05.751 --> 06:09.602
including them. Thank you. Okay, no further questions.

06:10.453 --> 06:13.760
Thank you. Does, does anyone else on council have any more questions or any more

06:14.260 --> 06:17.823
comments from those that are present? All right, so then I'll call for a motion.

06:19.059 --> 06:22.286
Mayor Pro Tempore, I'll make a motion. I move that the

06:22.786 --> 06:25.835
city council adopt a resolution of Eagle Mountain City, Utah,

06:25.947 --> 06:29.415
protesting the Red Cedar Corporation annexation petition filed

06:29.897 --> 06:33.076
with the town of Cedar Fort on July 27th, 2026.

06:33.574 --> 06:37.118
Second. All right, we have a motion from Council Member Wood

06:37.519 --> 06:41.320
and a second from Council Member Wright. Let's begin the vote with me.

06:41.513 --> 06:44.207
Yes. Council Member? Yes.

06:45.057 --> 06:49.419
Council Member Whiting? Yes. Council Member

06:49.547 --> 06:52.209
Wood? Yes. Council Member Hewish?

06:52.979 --> 06:56.315
Yes. Good job, you guys. I had a real hard time because we don't have

06:56.347 --> 06:57.485
our name plaques up.

07:00.100 --> 07:04.031
Thank you all for that. I'll call for a motion to adjourn. You need

07:04.531 --> 07:07.541
to announce that it's been, uh, what the vote was.

07:08.285 --> 07:11.802
Um, the, the vote, uh, was 5 to 0, passes.

07:14.020 --> 07:18.632
Will you entertain a motion, Mayor Pro Tem? I sure will. Motion to adjourn.

07:18.857 --> 07:22.248
Oh, second. We have a motion from Council

07:22.748 --> 07:25.516
Member Wood and a motion, a second from Council Member Wright. All in favor,

07:25.581 --> 07:29.071
please say aye. Aye. Aye. All right, we're adjourned

07:29.249 --> 07:32.891
at 5:23 PM.

07:33.636 --> 07:34.041
Thank you.
